title: Questions of Ideology
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: ideology_timer = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; old_ideology = ideology; ideology_timer = 18; changed = 0;
card-image: img/arbeiterbew.jpg
max-visits: 3
#subtitle: Setting the party's ideological direction.

= Questions of Ideology

The NSDAP is no monolith, and several ideological currents exist within it. What should be our primary ideological guidance for now?

[? if ideology != 0 : We have previously chosen a [+ ideology +] ideology. Changing it will likely have drawbacks. ?]

- @class_struggle: Preparing for a German Revolution against the Capitalist Weimar Government should be our primary goal.
- @centrist: Hitler's Populist strategies are the easiest path to power.
- @easy_discard

@class_struggle
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "left") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "left"; left_strength += 10; far_right_coalition -= 1; left_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 5; dnvp_relation -= 3; centrist_dissent += 2

The revolutionaries in the party reject cooperation with the establishment and capitalists, instead supporting a nationalist revolution against democracy.

@centrist
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "centrist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "centrist"; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 5

Supported by Hitler himself, this more Conservative ideological strand of National Socialism proposes using populist rhetoric to appeal to a wider range of voters.

@changed
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5

We have changed ideologies. Many in the party feel unmoored.
